<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="011" project="code-quality-and-assurance-r3">
  <metadata>
    <title>Assess shared server libs (Spaarke.Core / Dataverse / Scheduling, ~10k LOC)</title>
    <phase>1 Full Assessment</phase>
    <gate>blocked until 001,003</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Read-only Fable-verified assessment producing a design.md; no src/ or tests/ modification — STANDARD per task-create Step 3.5.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>fable</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Runs the quality-assessment workflow whose mandatory adversarial-verification stage is Fable (NFR-05).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>001,003</deps>
    <tags>assessment,quality,shared-server-libs</tags>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Run the quality-assessment Workflow READ-ONLY across the shared server libraries — src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core, Spaarke.Dataverse, Spaarke.Scheduling (~10k LOC). Produce a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design.md and append this surface's SCORECARD row. This surface roots the two-Dataverse-stacks question (NG1). Modify NO source.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer running the standing quality-assessment method. This surface underpins the BFF + plugins; the ServiceClient-vs-raw-HTTP stack split originates here. Follow ADRs strictly; the assessment is read-only.</role>
  <goal>projects/shared-server-libs-remediation-r1/design.md exists — a Fable-verified prioritized remediation design for the shared server libs, explicitly characterizing (but NOT resolving) the two-Dataverse-stacks question as NG1 — and notes/SCORECARD.md carries this surface's verified D1–D11 row.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-05 + design.md §7 (surface #2, roots the Dataverse-stack question). The BFF pass already confirmed DataverseServiceClientImpl vs raw-HTTP stack + always-failing casts; full stack unification is deferred as NG1 (a separate architecture project needing its own ADR — spec Out of Scope / FR-23). This assessment characterizes the shared-server debt and feeds the NG1 Idea, but does not unify the stacks.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Scheduling</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/quality-assessment.workflow.js</file>
      <file role="output">projects/shared-server-libs-remediation-r1/design.md</file>
      <file role="output">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Rubric D1–D11.</dependency>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">The quality-assessment workflow.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: READ-ONLY (NFR-03) — no src/ modification; only outputs are the surface design.md + SCORECARD row.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Scope: the Fable adversarial-verification pass is non-negotiable (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: MUST NOT propose unifying the two Dataverse stacks (NG1) in the remediation design — characterize it and route it to the NG1 Idea (FR-23); the BFF workstream only collapses the app-only downcast boilerplate (task 021).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Shared server library quality assessment</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/standards/CODE-QUALITY-RUBRIC.md</file>
      <file>projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/bff-api-cleanup-remediation-r1/design.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the rigor-level declaration (STANDARD + reason). Confirm "use a workflow" opt-in; load rubric + workflow.</step>
    <step order="1">Fan-out: one read-only finder per rubric dimension across the three shared-server packages, file:line evidence.</step>
    <step order="2">Mandatory Fable adversarial-verification stage; refute false positives; check test-only consumers + data-driven dispatch.</step>
    <step order="3">If verification refutes &gt;30% of findings or cannot confirm evidence, invoke the escalation trigger.</step>
    <step order="4">Synthesize projects/shared-server-libs-remediation-r1/design.md; explicitly mark the two-Dataverse-stacks item as NG1 (route to Idea, do not scope here).</step>
    <step order="5">Append this surface's verified D1–D11 row to notes/SCORECARD.md.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 011 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the Fable verification pass cannot confirm a finding's file:line evidence, or refutes &gt;30% of first-pass findings, STOP and report — do not synthesize a remediation design from unverified findings (NFR-05).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="doc">projects/shared-server-libs-remediation-r1/design.md</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/code-quality-and-assurance-r3/notes/SCORECARD.md (row appended)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, projects/shared-server-libs-remediation-r1/design.md exists, Fable-verified, with severity/LOC/effort/risk + tranche split.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the design, the two-Dataverse-stacks item is characterized and routed to NG1 (Idea) — NOT scoped as remediation here.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the run, notes/SCORECARD.md has this surface's verified row appended; no aggregate published.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no file under src/ was modified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-05. Feeds the NG1 Idea (FR-23). Remediation tasks deferred until this design exists.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
